// Three equal bars, 5:3, from a 1153 by 692 copy.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Desinoromantic flag"
  designer "pastelmemer (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/2017/http://pride-color-schemes.tumblr.com/post/146776374952/desinoromantic"
  note "The designer's own post was not found, so this is written from a secondary copy. The Tumblr blog pride-color-schemes posted the flag on 1 July 2016 (read from a 2017 Wayback snapshot of the address above), defining desinoromantic as 'liking' someone instead of 'loving' them romantically, with 'Term coined by: @pastelmemer' and 'Designed by: @pastelmemer'. Its image description reads 'a flag with three stripes. from top to bottom they are: pink, grey, green'. It gives no meanings or values."
  note "The colors are the medians of each bar in that post's image (a 1153 by 692 JPEG, fetched from Tumblr's media server): pink #ff93ff, grey #4b4b4b, green #94ffa1. The bars are equal and the proportion 5:3 is the image's."
}
palette {
  pink "#ff93ff"
  grey "#4b4b4b"
  green "#94ffa1"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars pink grey green
